l, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 737992, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01HPwdFQmKsHTPBad9VzK289", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 740129, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_014c5jZRWpt1dnUMDpE4qDuL", "tool": "open_pr", "args": {"head": "fix/money-half-even-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN (banker's rounding) in round_money per FIN-212", "body": "## Summary\nThe nightly build of payments-service was failing because `tests/test_money.py` expects banker's rounding, but `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`.\n\nThis PR changes `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, as specified in the function docstring and FIN-212.\n\n## Verification\n- `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` checks 2.675 -> 2.68 and 2.665 -> 2.66. Both match half-even rounding.\n- CI run `ci-0002` passed on commit `0a9452f727`, which is the branch head after merging latest main. An earlier run (`ci-0001`, commit `08d3cd5986`) also passed before the branch was updated.\n\n## Notes\n- The FIN-212 advisory lookup returned \"Unknown advisory\", so the spec reference rests on the docstring and the test. Please confirm FIN-212 is the correct reference.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-money-half-even-0a9452f727"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 741029, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_014c5jZRWpt1dnUMDpE4qDuL", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-money-half-even-0a9452f727", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 741029, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_014c5jZRWpt1dnUMDpE4qDuL", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 743334, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I opened PR #101 against main, with alex requested as reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n- **Fix:** In `src/money.py`, `round_money` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. I changed it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, which matches the docstring and `tests/test_money.py`. I checked the test values by hand: 2.675 \u2192 2.68 and 2.665 \u2192 2.66 are correct under half-even.\n- **Branch:** `fix/money-half-even-rounding`. The first PR attempt was rejected because the branch was behind main, so I merged main into the branch. That changed the head, so I reran CI.\n- **CI:** The first run (`ci-0001`, `08d3cd5986`) passed. The rerun on the updated head (`ci-0002`, `0a9452f727`) also passed. The PR cites the rerun.\n- **Not merged:** I did not merge the PR. Merging into main needs code-owner approval under policy.\n\nThe FIN-212 advisory lookup returned \"Unknown advisory\". The docstring and test still reference FIN-212, so I went ahead, and I flagged this in the PR for alex to confirm.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by reading the source and the test file to see what's expected.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01XyR4QanLrLzLgLK498FscU", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01T3xJdPYzWCoozW243efw7E", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01FqnpdDXtrg3S4Lvvu1dCoa", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The bug is clear: `src/money.py` uses `ROUND_HALF_UP`, but its docstring and the test both call for `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. I checked the test values by hand: 2.675 rounds to 2.68 and 2.665 rounds to 2.66 under half-even, so the test is correct. The FIN-212 advisory lookup failed, but the docstring already cites FIN-212, so I'll go ahead. Next I'll create the branch.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01LZNP5s8fR8mX5ciPBJzzeR", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-half-even-rounding", "from_ref": "main"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01UCH5QzwVZEmcf5dxdzAryA", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-half-even-rounding", "message": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN (banker's rounding) in round_money per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The fix is committed. Next I'll start CI on the branch.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01FpEJVQGsRNgo4EajbFsezW", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/money-half-even-rounding", "idempotency_key": "money-half-even-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01NEgABybRYRRrwW9vHZwqSc", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "CI passed on the branch. Now I'll open the pull request against main and request review from alex.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01BDmKPJVyAkL5JwuDmvMZow", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-half-even-rou